# Copy to backend/.env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# backend/.env is loaded automatically by both `go run ./cmd/api` and
# `go run ./cmd/adk-playground`. Variables already set in your shell take
# precedence over this file, so a one-off override still works:
#
#   MCDVOICE_LIVE=0 go run ./cmd/api
#
# Syntax: KEY=value, quotes optional, `export` tolerated, # starts a comment
# (a trailing comment needs a space before the #).

# --- Gemini (required) ------------------------------------------------------
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# Model override. Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash, which is the newest Flash that
# answers reliably on the free tier: gemini-2.5-flash 404s for keys created
# after its deprecation, and 3.7/3.8-flash frequently return 503.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# --- McDonald's Receipt Surveyer (Module 1) ---------------------------------
# MCDVOICE_LIVE=1 really completes the survey at mcdvoice.com and returns a
# usable validation code. Each run is irreversible and consumes the single use
# of a real receipt code, so leave it off while developing the agent.
# MCDVOICE_LIVE=0

# Your standing satisfaction rating, 1-5, submitted when the request does not
# specify one. Defaults to 5.
# MCDVOICE_RATING=5

# Dump each survey page's form controls to stderr. Use this on the first live
# run to capture the real question wording.
# MCDVOICE_DEBUG=0

# --- HTTP API ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=8080
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# --- Database (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Omit entirely to run with the in-memory store instead of Postgres.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/omstead?sslmode=disable
